{"title":"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of integers with the following properties:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1734dacd8bd88fcc1284df48edc9ca38c25b0c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 1, 2, \\dots, 2025 \\} \\subseteq S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ec3017bd97bd3c28f8f4ddda626a6a76217c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1a646aa72373ac52f63c2273ce82781d9b58a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a, b) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419af82307d4ee5c69a0fd298e3fcae1560514fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> If for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4f1f659ea5a289a0d8b827576e162351497439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafa4bf7cd6cfb72b9b7321311ea84b483d25224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is composite, then all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafa4bf7cd6cfb72b9b7321311ea84b483d25224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> contains all positive integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef8ce249f163b956eb1bc498f6e6699041ca784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots, n\\}\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9be6f7ae2670d327312a92eb498cf6b5c8f39f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is composite, we are done, so we assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is an odd prime.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd479a78b722cf08b2afc498c54e7cff64391dee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1\\ne 2^k\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c35291a0c669d59347a6171bc3190dc49764e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2\\ne 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba3a9dcc3b084e15997ed79b8ac9421bcfc953b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{v_2 (n+2)}, \\frac{n+2}{2^{v_2 (n+2)}}\\le n\\implies 2^{v_2 (n+2)}, \\frac{n+2}{2^{v_2 (n+2)}}\\in S\\implies n+2\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"505\" height=\"38\" />. Either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e303fcd7c7e53cd410ef0cb64f6b20bad80b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_2(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da00ff0d3874d10a6f496333a355a0c06bcf092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_2(n+2)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07cd9970c62602e66119698b48b603b773628f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{v_2(n)+v_2(n+2)}=2^{1+\\max(v_2(n), v_2(n+2))}=2\\cdot 2^{\\max(v_2(n), v_2(n+2))}\\le 2\\cdot \\frac{n+2}{3}\\le n\\implies 2^{v_2(n)+v_2(n+2)}\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"760\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/dea51cd366b53eebb3c59e7ec3a6c8544583b9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(n, n+2)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb44835445e6700223fec45d6b6ea306dd6de15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd\\left(\\frac{n}{2^{v_2(n)}}, \\frac{n+2}{2^{v_2(n+2)}}\\right)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"208\" height=\"45\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf6cff3a9cf204155af9c626c6df9322027daac3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{v_2(n)+v_2(n+2)}\\cdot \\frac{n}{2^{v_2(n)}}\\cdot \\frac{n+2}{2^{v_2(n+2)}}=n(n+2)\\in S\\implies n(n+2)+1=(n+1)^2\\in S\\implies n+1\\in S.\\]\" width=\"702\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/49445dffc0b1d64c98154d042723157c689a802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1=2^k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must be even, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d0e9e03d177bd9435904f590ef5365ac8c233b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k+1\\equiv 0\\pmod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"22\" />. Then we have the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef005eebcf5b3de2e114b2357661599fb8423587.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}}+1\\right)^2-1=2^{\\frac{k}{2}}\\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}}+2\\right)=2^{\\frac{k}{2}+1}\\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}-1}+1\\right)\\in S \\implies\\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}}+1\\right)^2\\in S\\]\" width=\"573\" height=\"35\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6efebec49c7653a1d1386cec5e964fbc7d2103.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2^{\\frac{k}{2}-1}\\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}}+1\\right)^2 = \\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}-1}+1\\right)\\left(2^k+1\\right)-1\\in S\\implies \\left(2^{\\frac{k}{2}-1}+1\\right)\\left(2^k+1\\right)\\in S\\implies 2^k+1\\in S,\\]\" width=\"768\" height=\"35\" />\nas desired.\n</p><p>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/41650cde3b4685bcbc8df01060a031b44b875d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1=2^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c877cdefa36f90cdf80f93dadc93cc77d19961a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa6d394520ed97a4a5db930ae3776d2b1045a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> be a positive integer. Then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12094d2ee931075bc68c574f36fa9b5a4e23771.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2^x-1)(2^k-1)-1=2^x\\left(2^k-2^{k-x}-1\\right)\\in S\\implies 2^k-1\\in S,\\]\" width=\"492\" height=\"21\" /> as desired.\n</p><p>Hence, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9ccd0fe7a9d4fdb479b935d4a025a36d98be4f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots, n\\}\\in S\\implies n+1\\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" />, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> spans all positive integers.\n</p><p>-mop\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO\" title=\"2025 USAJMO\">2025 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024748\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 236/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7793/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.528      1 -total\n 66.98%   11.740      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 31.75%    5.566      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31353:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024748 and revision id 245836. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}